# PAROLE / ePOS (TreeTagger)
#
# Danish PAROLE Part-of-Speech Tags as emitted by the TreeTagger Danish model,
# following the ePOS tag set (Asmussen 2015) which is based on the Danish PAROLE
# corpus (Keson 1998). The coarse part-of-speech is determined by the two-character
# CLASS at the head of each tag (the part before the first ':'); the remainder
# encodes positional morphological markers (nominal:verbal:additional).
#
# CLASS legend (first character = POS):
#   V=verb  A=adjective  L=numeral  N=noun(NP=proper)  P=pronoun  D=adverb
#   I=interjection  T=preposition  C=conjunction(CS=subordinating)  U=unique
#   (UI=infinitive marker 'at', US='som/der' marker)  E=lexical element
#   M=inflectional ending (bound morpheme)  X=residual(XS=symbol)
# The 'W' subclass marks word-formation/compound fragments of the respective POS.
# The Z* tags are punctuation (not part of the ePOS spec; mapping determined
# empirically by running the model: ZA apostrophe, ZD delimiter/bracket,
# ZH hyphen, ZS slash, ZI other punctuation) as is SENT.
#
# Source: extracted from the TreeTagger model using TT4J
__META_SOURCE_URL__=https\://korpus.dsl.dk/clarin/corpus-doc/pos-design.pdf
